84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (These upheavals have far-reaching implications for modern manufacturing, in addition to traditional commodities markets. Semiconductor manufacture, which is sometimes viewed as geographically centred in East Asia, remains heavily reliant on Middle Eastern supplies.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (Qatar produces nearly one-third of the world's helium, which is used to cool silicon wafers. ulphur derivatives are utilised in wafer cleaning and etching, whereas bromine, which is mostly supplied from the Dead Sea, is essential for chip production. These inputs pass through the same limited shipping routes that are currently under pressure.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
86 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (At the same time, energy dependence exacerbates the shock. Semiconductor centre like South Korea and Taiwan rely on imported LNG, much of which goes via Hormuz. As energy and input costs grow at the same time, chip production's economics degrade, injecting inflationary pressure into one of the world's most strategically essential industries.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 289 0 R
/E (What starts as a shipping interruption in the Gulf eventually spreads to the cost of AI infrastructure, consumer goods, and industrial gear, supporting the notion that contemporary supply chains are just as resilient as their weakest link.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
