100 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 298 0 R
/E (If the Strait of Hormuz stays limited, the ramifications will go far beyond oil markets. Industrial metals, fertilisers, and advanced manufacturing inputs will encounter tighter circumstances, not because they cannot be produced, but because they cannot be transferred efficiently on a large scale. In that regard, this is more than simply an oil shock. It's a logistical shock, and the consequences are just starting to be calculated.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
